fnm (1.39.0-1~ppa3) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * d/p/0002: refresh the lock again. The ~ppa2 lock still scans clean
    three weeks on -- no advisory has caught up with it -- but 45 crates
    had newer semver-compatible releases, so this takes them rather than
    letting the gap widen until a bump is forced. Notable only for jiff
    0.2 -> 1.0, nix 0.31 -> 0.32 and lzma-rust2 0.24 -> 0.25, all of
    which cargo resolved without a manifest change.
  * Upstream's full test suite passes against the refreshed lock, all 30
    tests, and the release build is warning-free. trivy reports nothing.
  * Still 1.39.0: that is upstream's current release.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:45:00 -0500

fnm (1.39.0-1~ppa2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Refresh the vendored crate set past 25 advisories. Upstream's
    Cargo.lock is the one 1.39.0 released with, and trivy reports 25
    advisories against it, one critical and six high.
  * d/p/0002: take the semver-compatible fixes cargo resolves on its
    own, which clears 22 of them: quinn-proto, rustls, rustls-webpki,
    hashbrown, tar, ring, idna (through url), time, bytes, tokio and
    rand. tar and ring are the ones that matter most here, since fnm
    unpacks downloaded Node.js tarballs and verifies the release
    server's certificate.
  * d/p/0001: take zip 9 for the remaining three, CVE-2026-115905,
    CVE-2026-115909 and CVE-2026-115906, which have no fix in the 2.x
    series upstream asks for. fnm's own use reaches none of the three,
    but the package now carries no crate with a known advisory. zip 9
    returns a Result from name() and mangled_name(), so the two call
    sites in src/archive/zip.rs propagate it.
  * Upstream's full test suite passes against the new lock, all 30
    tests, the zip extraction and Node install tests included.
  * d/make-orig-tarballs.sh applies debian/patches before cargo vendor,
    so the vendor component matches the lock the --frozen build uses.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 09:05:00 -0500

fnm (1.39.0-1~ppa1~ubuntu26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging of upstream release 1.39.0, for
    ppa:pillarsdotnet/ppa.
  * Every crate in Cargo.lock travels in the orig-vendor component
    tarball; crates that only build for Windows, macOS or WebAssembly
    are stubbed to their manifests there.
  * Upstream's test suite needs network access (it downloads Node.js
    releases), so the package build smoke-tests the binary instead.
  * Manual page generated with help2man; bash, zsh and fish completions
    generated by the built binary itself.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Sat, 18 Oct 2026 22:10:00 -0400
